# Frontend Conventions

## Next.js App Router
- Use the App Router (`app/` directory)
- Server Components are the default - use `'use client'` only when needed
- Use `loader.ts` files to organize server-side data fetching logic (project convention)
- Keep page components thin - extract logic to hooks and utilities

## React Patterns
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use TypeScript for all components with proper type definitions
- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility

## State Management (Zustand)
- Store definitions live in `lib/store.ts`
- Store uses `devtools` and `persist` middleware
- Can only be used in Client Components (add `'use client'` directive)
- Keep stores focused and split by domain if needed
- Use selectors (e.g., `selectActiveConversation`) to minimize re-renders

## Effect Library
- Use Effect for complex async operations and error handling
- Prefer Effect pipelines for data transformation
- Handle errors explicitly using Effect's error channel

## Styling (Tailwind CSS v4)
- Use Tailwind utility classes directly in JSX
- CSS variables for colors/theme are defined in `globals.css`
- Extract repeated patterns to reusable component abstractions

## Routing
- Routes are defined by the file system in `app/` directory
- Dashboard is at `/dashboard`
- Root `/` redirects to dashboard
